 "rules": [
  "Cabin ACs run at 25 to 26 C; hall ACs run only during events and cabin ACs go off by the event start.",
  "GPU training jobs are scheduled outside event hours; short inference or CAD work is fine any time.",
  "Kettle and microwave are on separate circuits and not used together during an event peak; no geysers or heaters anywhere.",
  "Battery chargers are current-limited and bulk-charge at night; after a daytime outage expect up to 1.3 kW of recharge on top of the running load.",
  "An energy monitor with per-phase clamps at the main DB shows live demand on the reception screen; at 9 kW it flags, at 9.5 kW the hall AC 2 contactor drops out."
 ],
